00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:14.870 align:start position:0%
in this breakthrough you could say that  physicists have taken a new angle on  subatomic particles called neutrinos  neutrinos are born in nuclear  interactions and they come in three  different types or flavors they also  change from one flavor to another as  they zip along at just about light speed  these so called neutrino oscillations  are described by six parameters the  three mass differences among the  neutrinos and three abstract mixing  angles this year physicists with the  daya Bay neutrino reactor experiments in  China measured the last of these  parameters an angle known as theta one  three they showed that it was about nine  degrees the fact that all three of the  mixing angles are not zero means that  it's possible that neutrinos and  antineutrinos  oscillate slightly differently that in  turn could help explain how the universe  generated so much matter in so little  antimatter so this result really shows  that neutrino physics has a very bright  future it's also the most important  physics result ever to come out of China  some physicists say so for those reasons  the measurement of the last neutrino  mixing angle is one of our top ten  breakthroughs in beer  you
 

